## Getting Started

Run these in order to set up your database and start developing:

1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "contract:emit"}}` to emit Prisma Next contract artifacts.
{{#if useLocalMongo}}
1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:up"}}` to start the local MongoDB replica set (detached).
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq provider "postgres")}}
1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:init"}}` to initialize the PostgreSQL database.
{{/if}}
1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "migration:plan"}}` to write a migration plan from your contract.
1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "migrate"}}` to apply the planned migration.
1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:seed"}}` to insert sample users.
1. Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "dev"}}` to start the dev server.

{{#if useLocalMongo}}
The local MongoDB binds to a per-project port baked into `.env` and persists data in `.mongo-data/`. Use `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:down"}}` to stop it (data preserved) or `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:reset"}}` to wipe `.mongo-data/`.
{{/if}}

## Scripts

- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "dev"}}`: start the local dev server with hot reload.
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "build"}}`: {{#if (eq packageManager "deno")}}type-check the app with Deno.{{else}}{{#if (eq packageManager "bun")}}type-check the app for Bun.{{else}}typecheck and compile.{{/if}}{{/if}}
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "start"}}`: {{#if (eq packageManager "deno")}}run the server directly from `src/index.ts` with Deno.{{else}}{{#if (eq packageManager "bun")}}run the server directly from `src/index.ts` with Bun.{{else}}run the compiled server from `dist/`.{{/if}}{{/if}}

## Prisma Next

Prisma Next setup is scaffolded in:

- `prisma/contract{{#if (eq authoring "typescript")}}.ts{{else}}.prisma{{/if}}`
- `prisma-next.config.ts`
- `src/lib/prisma.ts`

Database helper scripts in `package.json`:

- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "contract:emit"}}`: emit contract artifacts after contract changes.
{{#if (eq provider "postgres")}}
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:init"}}`: initialize database state.
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:update"}}`: update database state.
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:verify"}}`: verify the database matches the contract.
{{/if}}
{{#if useLocalMongo}}
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:up"}}`: start the local MongoDB replica set with `mongodb-memory-server`.
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:down"}}`: stop the local MongoDB process (data preserved).
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:reset"}}`: stop and wipe `.mongo-data/`.
{{/if}}
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "migration:plan"}}`: write a migration plan.
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "migrate"}}`: apply a planned migration.
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "db:seed"}}`: insert sample users.

For provider-specific Prisma Next reference docs, see `prisma-next.md`. Prisma Next skills live in the upstream `skills/` directory: https://github.com/prisma/prisma-next/tree/main/skills.

Node-based Prisma Next projects expect Node.js 24 LTS or newer.

The template includes a basic `User` model and a sample `GET /users` endpoint.
